# ============================================================================
#  The Press Room — what never goes in git.
#
#  These are runtime state and raw material. The scripts recreate the folders
#  they need on first run; nothing here is shipped.
# ============================================================================

# YOUR CONFIG. It names paths on your machine and points at your credential
# files. Commit press-room.config.example.json instead.
press-room.config.json

# RAW, UNGATED, OR SENSITIVE-IN-PASSING material — the most important block here.
# .staging/ holds raw transcript text; inbox/ holds quarantined inbound mail;
# reading-room/ is the composer's rebuilt world; answers/ and drafts/ are pre-send;
# state/ holds ledgers, the LIVE flag, crash + shift logs, and drill runs.
.staging/
inbox/
reading-room/
answers/
drafts/
state/

# GENERATED OUTPUT — rebuilt from the committed sources.
out/

# THE GATED, PUBLISHABLE ARTIFACTS (digests/, facts/, receipts/) are meant to be
# committed once you are happy with them, so they are NOT ignored. Uncomment to
# keep them local instead:
# digests/
# facts/
# receipts/

# Your real denylist. The example ships; yours, with your names and paths, does
# not. Comment this out if you deliberately want to publish your denylist.
redaction/REDACTION.md

# Working-root stop flags.
PAUSE
KILL-*
HOLD
HOLD-*

# Junk.
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
